edition sheet didn't seem to do anything funky at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","user":"BronzeDog","date":". 04-01-2016, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:03:08-07:00","id":857372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=857358#post857358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that was weird. This time I had my book pdfs open and when I downloaded a new copy, Acrobat stopped responding, but I was able to go into task manager and stop it, rather than have everything freeze up. I think I might uninstall and reinstall Acrobat as my next step.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and the 1st edition sheet didn't seem to do anything funky at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something to do with the newer version of Acrobat; I've had it freeze, lock up and then crash with no rhyme or reason for some time now. Unless I save regularly it also deletes all my work. Quite annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/a