ted the 2nd Ed Changeling sheets for the new version. I had someone send me some of the info on the changes, so hopefully I got everyone ok. If you spot anything wrong, let me know.<br /> <br /> Here are the links:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_1-Page_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_2-Page_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/CtL/CtL_2ndED_4-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...nteractive.pdf</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great work! Thank you for the updated sheet. One minor correction at the bottom -- Clarity is now equal to the character's Wits + Composure. Also, the preview talks about Clarity functioning more like the health track, with the Clarity damage moving from left to right like regular damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","name":"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:03:28-08:00","id":1174376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jojo11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174334#post1174334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great work! Thank you for the updated sheet. One minor correction at the bottom -- Clarity is now equal to the character's Wits + Composure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'll work on getting that fixed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jojo11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174334#post1174334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the preview talks about Clarity functioning more like the health track, with the Clarity damage moving from left to right like regular damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I'd heard that, but in talking with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> , he sent me this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way Touchstone attachment is described is thus:<br /> 'Write Touchstones alongside your character's Clarity track. Count boxes from the left equal to your character\u2019s Composure + 1, and write your first Touchstone next to that box. For instance, if your character has Composure 3, you would write the Touchstone next to the fourth box from the left.' </div> </div> </div>I don't see how we could do with a horizontal Clarity track. So, I went for the old style horizontal track. I'm open to suggestion though if there is a better way...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:14:07-08:00","id":1174382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174376#post1174376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'd heard that, but in talking with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> , he sent me this:<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see how we could do with a horizontal Clarity track. So, I went for the old style horizontal track. I'm open to suggestion though if there is a better way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make the track horizontal with the lines for writing touchstones at an angle (like 30 or 45 degrees?) coming off of each one (if you can do that in an editable pdf)? Not sure how well that fits on the sheet though, it might be too wide for the current 3 column design.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:37:11-08:00","id":1174387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174382#post1174382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make the track horizontal with the lines for writing touchstones at an angle (like 30 or 45 degrees?) coming off of each one (if you can do that in an editable pdf)? Not sure how well that fits on the sheet though, it might be too wide for the current 3 column design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've done some vertical form field columns before, so I don't think it's impossible. I'm just not sure how to make something like fit properly with the sheet layout. Plus, the check boxes themselves aren't very wide, so the text would be pretty tiny... I could space out the boxes and dots somewhat, but it still wouldn't be a lot of room to write.<br /> <br /> I can play around with it an see...<br /> <br /> I wonder why they designed it that way though? Seems like an odd choice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:40:13-08:00","id":1174388,"title":"","content":"It's probably designed purely from a gameplay standpoint, without the character sheet in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:55:11-08:00","id":1174392,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe have both? The Clarity &quot;health track&quot; in one place and in another have the vertical Humanity-style track where you can mark Touchstones?</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","user":"jojo11","date":". 01-08-2018, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","name":"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:58:00-08:00","id":1174394,"title":"","content":"Duplicate post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","user":"jojo11","date":". 01-08-2018, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","name":"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:20:04-08:00","id":1174487,"title":"","content":"An idea; what about changing out the circles for a vertical oriented health-box, with two columns of boxes? Touchstones are attached to the Clarity box that is equal to Composure + 1, and any Touchstones gained after are put to the right of that box (or above, in this case). By having the Clarity and Touchstones be vertical, you retain the look and ease of use but still allow Clarity to go even higher than 10. Bear in mind, Clarity can be permanently increased by finding Icons, literal pieces of a Changeling's past and memory, so it's not simply stuck at a Changeling's attributes and Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-09-2018, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T04:39:40-08:00","id":1174520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jojo11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174392#post1174392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe have both? The Clarity &quot;health track&quot; in one place and in another have the vertical Humanity-style track where you can mark Touchstones?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of this too, but with both tracks, at the end of the day you end up taking up sheet space for no net gain vs having 'health boxes' attached to the vertical track. I suppose it might be more readable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T05:10:20-08:00","id":1174524,"title":"","content":"Maybe have a touchstone section under it to detail them and just write T or T1, T2 under the square like you would the wound penalties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T08:36:07-08:00","id":1174557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174388#post1174388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably designed purely from a gameplay standpoint, without the character sheet in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it... I'll be curious to see what they do when it comes time for a character sheet...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174487#post1174487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea; what about changing out the circles for a vertical oriented health-box, with two columns of boxes? Touchstones are attached to the Clarity box that is equal to Composure + 1, and any Touchstones gained after are put to the right of that box (or above, in this case). By having the Clarity and Touchstones be vertical, you retain the look and ease of use but still allow Clarity to go even higher than 10. Bear in mind, Clarity can be permanently increased by finding Icons, literal pieces of a Changeling's past and memory, so it's not simply stuck at a Changeling's attributes and Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think removing the circles and having two rows or vertical boxes? And having Clarity just be the dots in a horizontal row?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:03:12-08:00","id":1174590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>De_K47</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1174524#post1174524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe have a touchstone section under it to detail them and just write T or T1, T2 under the square like you would the wound penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might be the quickest and easiest solution. If you turn Clarity into a health track, that should free up some space to add a Touchstone list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","name":"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T11:16:15-08:00","id":1174597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__