"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T14:47:12-08:00","id":1176385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jojo11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1175965#post1175965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. I think it's easy enough to write a touchstone number under the corresponding box and then just number the list below for reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, seems like it could work pretty nice that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T13:32:49-08:00","id":1177672,"title":"","content":"I have a request, for a True Fae Title character sheet. It seems like in 2e, thankfully, each Title has the same traits whether it's Manifesting as an Actor, Prop, Realm, etc. And they're very like the standard changeling. I beg humbly that you, if you have some time to do so, craft a Title sheet. Each Manifestation is likely to share the same traits, though it differs from the other titles of a True Fae itself, and in theory, a given gentry can exist with between 1 and 5 sheets. I am by no means making demands, just giving a suggestion of what a useful Gentry character sheet might have.<br /> <br /> The differences... firstly, concept is fully covered by titles, so instead of that and Kith and court, there should be room for a list of all 0-5 titles the far core has, and it's true name. Seeming is still necessary, as are needle and thread. Aspirations should have the Craving and two additional aspirations (one of which could be a Keeper one).<br /> <br /> Attributes and skills should be to ten, and maybe skills like an archangel.<br /> <br /> Merits is normal, with the line next to it to specify details like if it's ironside etc.<br /> <br /> Thankfully the sheet doesn't need space for full lists of contracts, it just needs a spot for 6 Regalia (not preset, like skills and attributes, because some storytellers might make up new regalia) and that should give more space.<br /> <br /> No clarity, more health. <br /> <br /> Wyrd and frailties, and a lot of space for pledges. Pledges is the biggest part of any given Gentry, so extra space would be perfect.<br /> <br /> From that character sheet, I think a given storyteller can staple it together/save in same folder all the titles of a true fae, and manifest them however they want. Iirc these are all the pertinent details of a given title that will translate over regardless of its manifestation. And each Title has it's own traits, so each will need a character sheet. But the finer details of your excellent 4 page sheets are flexible and based on any given moment for Gentry, so each Title should need more than a one page sheet.<br /> <br /> I beg you man, once you have time, I would love to have official Mr. Gone sheets for Titles. Groups playing the Game of Immortals could trade these sheets like trading cards when they win or lose, adjusting traits and rewriting data. Sts of standard games would know the traits of a Keeper whether it's manifest as a realm or actor or prop. And it gives the ST a secret pattern they can keep hold of when manifesting a Keeper. Your work is incredible, I don't think anyone is better at this than you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 01-20-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T14:37:58-08:00","id":1177690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1177672#post1177672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The differences... firstly, concept is fully covered by titles, so instead of that and Kith and court, there should be room for a list of all 0-5 titles the far core has, and it's true name. Seeming is still necessary, as are needle and thread. Aspirations should have the Craving and two additional aspirations (one of which could be a Keeper one).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait I thought Gentry didn't have Anchor's beyond Aspirations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T15:04:07-08:00","id":1177946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1177672#post1177672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beg you man, once you have time, I would love to have official Mr. Gone sheets for Titles. Groups playing the Game of Immortals could trade these sheets like trading cards when they win or lose, adjusting traits and rewriting data. Sts of standard games would know the traits of a Keeper whether it's manifest as a realm or actor or prop. And it gives the ST a secret pattern they can keep hold of when manifesting a Keeper. Your work is incredible, I don't think anyone is better at this than you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww...thanks for the kind words. I appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sure, I could probably add this to my to-do list. Maybe once I get the sheet for the new version finalized I'll see about doing this one. And if you think of anything else for this one, let me know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:03:04-07:00","id":1212735,"title":"","content":"Are Approaches and character specific breaking-points still a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T16:34:32-07:00","id":1212833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Borne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/845335-character-sheet?p=1212735#post1212735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Approaches and character specific breaking-points still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're no longer <i>the entirety of the game's consistent breaking points</i>, but yes, as with other gamelines there's explicit room to adjust the table of examples to suit your characters and games.<br /> <br /> Approaches aren't as granular as they were in the playtest draft, but the Bargain of a Court can fill a similar role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}